            <div xml:id="d101">

                <pb facs="0211" n="111" sameAs="frus:frus1934v01/pg111"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A14/664a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chairman of the American
                        Delegation</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1934-06-07T19:00:00-04:00">June 7, 1934—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>429. Your 883, June 7, 3 p.m. Every effort is being made to secure favorable
                    action by the Senate on the Treaty and it appears probable that advice and
                    consent to ratification will be given next week.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
